  "interpretation": "Proper deconfounding (Model A/B) yields ZERO false-positive imagery reliability when the video-specific cue/video response is <=0.5x the imagery response, but 25-50% false-positive reliability at comparable (1.0x) magnitude, because a video-specific cue response is consistent across repetitions and the reliability estimator cannot distinguish it from imagery. The naive late-window model (C) leaks even at 0.25x. The ACTUAL cue-response magnitude in VC is unknown and can only be measured from raw BOLD, which is infeasible here.",
